Upon completing the Nessus room, I gained practical experience in vulnerability assessment using one of the industry's leading vulnerability management platforms. The room introduced the complete vulnerability scanning process, from configuring scans to analysing results and prioritising remediation efforts.

Topics Covered
Introduction to Nessus
Learned the purpose and capabilities of Nessus as a vulnerability assessment tool.
Understood the role of vulnerability scanning within an organisation's security programme.
Explored how automated vulnerability assessments support proactive security management.
Nessus Installation and Configuration
Gained familiarity with the Nessus interface and dashboard.
Learned how to configure scan policies and assessment settings.
Understood how to manage scan targets and authentication options.
Host Discovery and Enumeration
Performed network discovery to identify live hosts.
Learned how Nessus detects operating systems, services, and installed applications.
Explored service and version identification techniques.
Vulnerability Scanning
Configured and executed vulnerability scans against target systems.
Learned how Nessus identifies security weaknesses using its plugin database.
Explored different scan templates for various assessment objectives.
Analysing Scan Results
Learned how to interpret vulnerability findings.
